values ('a2b3c4d5-6e7f-4a17-8b96-0c1d2e3f4a07', 'hospitality-marketing', 'Hospitality Marketing', 'This course prepares students to analyze, design, execute, measure, and improve marketing for hotels, resorts, restaurants, clubs, events, attractions, and related service organizations. Students use consumer research and market intelligence to select targets, position brands, design offers and guest journeys, coordinate integrated communications, manage digital and distribution channels, build CRM and loyalty programs, evaluate pricing and promotions, protect reputation, and allocate resources using experiments and financial evidence. U.S. truth-in-advertising, review, privacy, accessibility, and AI governance issues are embedded throughout, with global and cultural contexts considered where relevant.');

